r).","The 11 covering analysts target $21.32 on average, 67% above the price, well away from the model's fair value.","The price implies 13.4% annual cash-flow growth, 3pp less than the model expects."],"prof":["ROIC of 1% falls short of the cost of capital of 10.7%, so growth at these returns destroys value.","It runs a 24% gross margin and converts 32% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.51x.","ROE of 18% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.4x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 68pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.9% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.47).","Its debt comes due soon (maturity wall about 1.7 years out), so refinancing terms matter."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 38.1% over 3 years and 21.4% over 5 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 39%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 1.0% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 68.2% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.8% trend).","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 10.7% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 53, clearing the bar for a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and institutions hold 86%.","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 5 sales over the past year, net $1.8M sold.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.2% (0.3% in dividends).","The share count has grown 31.8% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 10 consecutive years."],"people":["With about 2,620 employees, each generates about $790K of revenue, 1.3x the Basic Materials median, and revenue has grown 9.7% a year across its filed history."